# Integer8 minimum and maximum values

Verifies the int8 boundary values through the complete CLI pipeline. The
maximum is expressible as a literal; the minimum is derived by subtracting
one from the largest negative literal because a negated minimum-magnitude
literal is validated unsigned first, consistent with int16 and int64.

>>> source
ceiling: int8 = 127
floor: int8 = -127
unit: int8 = 1

// Verifies the largest int8 literal prints unchanged.
print(ceiling)

// Verifies the int8 minimum is reachable through checked arithmetic.
minimum: int8 = floor - unit
print(minimum)

<<< stdout
127
-128

<<< stderr
